WEBVTT

NOTE
Unpublished R311 script/caption CONCEPT for an ORIGINAL 42-second source explainer.
No video encoded/hosted, no audio recorded, no autoplay.
Caption text should be aligned with real future narration in QA.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Imagine choosing between two ordinary photographs.
You make your selection.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
The researcher hands back an image.
But the image has changed.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Could you notice? In choice-blindness studies,
some people did not.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Some even described why they preferred
the picture they had not chosen.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
That reveals a limit in these studies,
not a universal failure of memory.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
See the sources. Keep the choice
and the explanation separate.
